libkrun: the display's refresh rate, live, and screen updates paced to it.
DisplayBackend::refresh(index) hands the caller a DisplayRefresh; its set(hz) changes the rate the
display's EDID says and, while a GPU device shows the display, raises VIRTIO_GPU_EVENT_DISPLAY so the
guest reads the display again (the rate it already has changes nothing). A fenced RESOURCE_FLUSH is
answered at the display's next refresh: the guest's display waits for that answer before it reports
the frame shown, so a guest kernel without virtio-gpu vblank (before Linux 6.19) is paced at the
display's rate, as a real display paces it (Sentinel: DESIGN.md §6, §16).

